msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-rockblock.rst:9
#: d274772a8f01402fa580c62d92454a2f
msgid "The `RockBLOCK <https://www.groundcontrol.com/products/>`__ satellite modem allows for a global (including polar regions) MAVLink connection to an ArduPilot vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-rockblock.rst:12
#: eb4d9daa667c4114a9a9947797aacef6
msgid "Due to the very low datarate of the RockBLOCK, there are a few key limitations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-rockblock.rst:14
#: 90891e74be634cc699b4f3ee7f2f5006
msgid "A single `HIGH_LATENCY2 <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#HIGH_LATENCY2>`__ packet will be sent every ``RCK_PERIOD`` sec. This will give basic position and status information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-rockblock.rst:15
#: 752fb5f351c44c03afa2d516aab07340
msgid "No heartbeats, statustexts, parameters and waypoints will be sent from the vehicle to the GCS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-rockblock.rst:16
#: 57bb7024e2b1476b8230d5cd0b73e27d
msgid "The RockBLOCK only sends a subset of MAVlink messages (see below list) from the GCS to Vehicle. Parameters and waypoints will not be sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-rockblock.rst:17
#: 03331cd672f84e1d819de18062e77823
msgid "Only 1 command message can be sent per ``RCK_PERIOD`` from the GCS to vehicle. Any additional commands will overwrite the previous command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-rockblock.rst:19
#: 9cc2a985ece6418889c1d23eb2a9e8b9
msgid "In practice, this means the RockBLOCK can only be used whilst monitoring a vehicle during automated flight modes. Any sort of manual control (outside of low-rate GUIDED mode \"fly to\" locations) is not possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-rockblock.rst:21
#: 8b5b8af32a8248daba96ec502c7a45ae
msgid "If desired, the RockBlock can automatically activate on loss-of-GCS-telemetry. This is done by setting the ``RCK_FORCEHL`` parameter to 2. The RockBLOCK will then automatically activate when telemetry is lost for ``RCK_TIMEOUT`` seconds. When telemetry is restored, the RockBLOCK will deactivate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-rockblock.rst:25
#: b5619c0b98134ab8b18002b21fb6cdc3
msgid "The RockBLOCK 9704 is the current and recommended model. It has a faster transmit time and lower power consumption than the 9603 model."
msgstr ""

